sentences.l:
But she, the mother now,
was tearing her hair, and away from her flung her sleek veil
far off, and cried out very loudly, having caught sight of her child;

Let me beg this man, wanton, mighty-working,
if somehow he will show respect to my age and pity
old age;

and indeed for him too a father of this kind has been made,
Peleus, who begot him and was rearing him to become a woe
for the Trojans;

For all of them I do not grieve so much, grieved though I am,
as for one, for whom a sharp grief will carry me down within Hades,
Hector;

The voice of my revered mother-in-law I heard, and in me myself
in my breast leaps my heart up to my mouth, and below, my knees
stiffen;

And now you, to the house of Hades beneath the hidden places of the earth,
are going, but me in hateful grief you leave
a widow in the halls;

For even if he escape the tearful war of the Achaeans,
always surely for him toil and sorrows hereafter
will be;

he is utterly bowed down, and his cheeks are wet with tears,
and in need the child goes up to his father’s companions,
one by the cloak tugging, another by the tunic;

And tearful goes up the child to his widowed mother,
Astyanax, who formerly upon the knees of his own father
marrow alone used to eat and the rich fat of sheep;

but whenever sleep took him, and he stopped playing the child,
he would sleep in beds, in the arms of a nurse,
on a soft couch, having filled his heart with good things;

But now you, beside the curved ships, apart from your parents,
quick-moving worms will eat, after the dogs have had their fill,
naked;
